ctives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use basic information in simple situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands basic information in English texts according to the communicative topics of this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands basic information in English texts according to the communicative topics of this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands basic information in English texts according to the communicative topics of this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands basic information in English texts according to the communicative topics of this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Completes simple dialogues by the addition or selection of appropriate language according to the communicative functions of this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Completes simple dialogues by the addition or selection of appropriate language according to the communicative functions of this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Completes simple dialogues by the addition or selection of appropriate language according to the communicative functions of this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Completes simple dialogues by the addition or selection of appropriate language according to the communicative functions of this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Some, Much, Many and A Lot Of", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Some</span>, <span class=\"strong\">much</span>, <span class=\"strong\">many</span> and <span class=\"strong\">a lot of</span> are quantifiers. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":\"3\",\"columns\":\"4\",\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Question</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Statement</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> With Count Nouns</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> How many books? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"so many books<br />a lot of books\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"not many books\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> With Non-count Nouns</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> How much water? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"so much water<br />a lot of water\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"not much water\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "  You use <span class=\"strong\">some</span> with count nouns (in the singular) or with non-count nouns (in the plural) to talk about the number of items. <br /> You use <span class=\"strong\">many</span> with count nouns to talk about the number of items. <br /> You use <span class=\"strong\">much</span> with non-count nouns to talk about the amount or quantity of an item. <br /> You use <span class=\"strong\">a lot of</span> with count and non-count nouns. <br /> Note: You use <span class=\"strong\">many</span> and <span class=\"strong\">much</span> with <span class=\"strong\">so</span> in statements, or use <span class=\"strong\">a lot of</span> instead.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn1le05ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Read the short dialogue with a partner. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Now, write a dialogue. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You are at a cafe.  Offer your partner a dessert and drink. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Accept or refuse the off